\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The integral measure}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The integration measure uses #{\extd}, the same symbol as the
exterior derivative. Mathematical physics writes #{dx} or #{d\mu},
and geometric calculus writes a directed measure #{\extd^{n}x}. The
integral sign is what marks the measure. A linear change of
reference volume is otherwise the same statement.}
